.TH std::is_sufficiently_aligned 3 "2026.11.10" "http://cppreference.com" "C++ Standard Libary"
.SH NAME
std::is_sufficiently_aligned \- std::is_sufficiently_aligned

.SH Synopsis
Defined in header <memory>
template< std::size_t N, class T >       (since C++26)
bool is_sufficiently_aligned( T* ptr );

Checks whether the pointer ptr points to an object whose alignment has a value of at least
N.

The behavior is undefined if ptr does not point to an object of type T (ignoring
cv-qualification at every level).

.SH Return value

true if ptr points to an object that has alignment at least N; otherwise false.

.SH Exceptions

Throws nothing.

.SH Notes

std::is_sufficiently_aligned can be used as a precondition to std::assume_aligned.

       Feature-test macro          Value    Std             Feature
__cpp_lib_is_sufficiently_aligned 202411L (C++26) std::is_sufficiently_aligned

.SH Possible implementation

template<std::size_t N, class T>
bool is_sufficiently_aligned(T* ptr)
{
    return std::bit_cast<std::uintptr_t>(ptr) % N == 0;
}

